.TH WPS-COPY 1 "2026-10-28" "wps-clip-bridge 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wps\-copy \- put a WPS recent document on the X11 clipboard as a real file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wps\-copy
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B wps\-copy
\fINUMBER\fR | \fIKEYWORD\fR
.br
.B wps\-copy \-f
\fIFILE\fR [\fIFILE\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wps\-copy
lists the documents recently opened by WPS for Linux (read from
.IR ~/.config/Kingsoft/Office.conf )
and writes the chosen file to the X11 clipboard as a real file object,
so it can be pasted into the desktop, WeChat, a mail client, etc.
.PP
This exists because the "Copy" action on the WPS document list is a no-op
on Linux: it takes ownership of the CLIPBOARD selection but never writes any
data into it, so nothing can be pasted anywhere.
.PP
With no arguments the most recently modified document is copied.
The clipboard is held by a background service, so closing any window does
not invalidate the copied file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-list [\fIKEYWORD\fR ...]
List recent documents: index, type, size, modification time and full path.
Pinned documents are marked with a star; the index numbers are exactly what
\fBwps\-copy \fIN\fR accepts.
.B \-\-pinned
limits the list to pinned documents and
.B \-\-json
emits machine-readable records (path, name, dir, kind, source, size, mtime,
when, pinned).
.TP
.B \-\-pin \fIFILE\fR ... / \-\-unpin \fIFILE\fR ...
Pin or unpin documents so they stay at the top of the picker list.
Without arguments,
.B \-\-pin
prints the documents currently pinned.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-file \fIFILE\fR ...
Copy the given files instead of consulting the recent list.
Multiple files are allowed.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-gui
Open the graphical picker window.
.TP
.B \-\-start
Start the background service now, so that a re-login is not required
right after installation.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Stop the background service.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
打印自检报告：会话类型、依赖、最近文档各数据源的命中数、兜底源是否存在、
三个后台进程的状态。列表为空或被说「没反应」时先看这个。
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-status
Show the state of the background service, hotkey and picker window.
.TP
.B \-\-migrate
Remove a previous manual installation (autostart entries, stray processes
and leftover runtime files) so that it cannot fight with this package.
Run once after installing if you had been running the scripts by hand.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wps-clip-bridge/config.ini
User configuration. The hotkey is set here, see
.BR wps\-copy\-hotkey (1).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/wps-clip-bridge/
Log files (bridge.log, hotkey.log, daemon.log).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wps-clip-bridge/
Locks and the copy-request file; cleared on logout.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Copy the newest recent document:
.PP
.RS 4
wps\-copy
.RE
.PP
List candidates, then copy the third one:
.PP
.RS 4
wps\-copy \-\-list
.br
wps\-copy 3
.RE
.PP
Copy every file whose name contains a keyword:
.PP
.RS 4
wps\-copy 报告
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wps\-copy\-gui (1),
.BR wps\-copy\-hotkey (1),
.BR wps\-clip\-bridge\-daemon (1)
